      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if a user doesn\u0027t have a default_project_id? It seems that instead of getting a project scoped token you return a domain scoped token. I don\u0027t like that the type of token changes based on a user attribute, instead of the request being different. If we really want this to only work for 1 project for each user, the lack of default_project_id should cause this to fail.",
